  <details class="legend" open>
    <summary>How Crapless Craps works</summary>
    <ul>
      <li><b>Come-out</b> — a 7 wins the Pass Line. <i>Every other total</i>, including 2, 3, 11 and 12, becomes the point. There is no way to lose a Pass Line bet on the come-out.</li>
      <li><b>The catch</b> — 11 is a point here, not an instant winner. In standard craps a come-out 11 pays immediately; in Crapless you now have to roll it again before a 7, which happens only 1 time in 4.</li>
      <li><b>After the point</b> — exactly like standard craps: roll the point again before a 7 and the Pass Line wins 1:1; a 7 first is a seven-out and the Pass Line loses.</li>
      <li><b>No Don't side</b> — Don't Pass and Don't Come aren't offered. With no craps numbers to win on, there's nothing for them to bet against.</li>
    </ul>
  </details>

  <details class="legend">
    <summary>Bet reference</summary>
    <ul>
      <li><b>Pass Line</b> — 7 wins on the come-out; anything else is the point. Pays 1:1 when the point repeats before a 7.</li>
      <li><b>Odds</b> — true-odds bet behind the Pass Line or a Come bet, no house edge. Max {{ craplessOdds.oddsMult[2] }}x on 2, 3, 4, 10, 11 and 12, {{ craplessOdds.oddsMult[5] }}x on 5/9, {{ craplessOdds.oddsMult[6] }}x on 6/8.</li>
      <li><b>Come</b> — the Pass Line rules again, started mid-hand: 7 wins, any other total becomes that bet's own point.</li>
      <li><b>Place</b> — on any of the ten numbers. Pays {{ craplessOdds.placeOddsStr[2] }} on 2/12, {{ craplessOdds.placeOddsStr[3] }} on 3/11, {{ craplessOdds.placeOddsStr[4] }} on 4/10, {{ craplessOdds.placeOddsStr[5] }} on 5/9, {{ craplessOdds.placeOddsStr[6] }} on 6/8.</li>
      <li><b>Buy</b> — on 4, 5, 6, 8, 9 and 10 only (this table doesn't book Buy bets on the extreme numbers). Pays true odds minus a {{ craplessOdds.buyCommissionPct }}% commission charged up front.</li>
      <li><b>Field, Any Seven, Any Craps, Hardways</b> — identical to standard craps. They don't depend on the come-out rules, so their payouts and edges don't change. Any Craps still means a one-roll 2, 3 or 12.</li>
      <li><b>Come-out roll</b> — Place, Buy, Hardway bets and Come-bet odds are <i>off</i> on the come-out unless you tick "Bets work on the come-out".</li>
      <li><b>After a win</b> — take a winning Place/Buy/Hardway bet down, leave it up, or press it (winnings go back on the bet in whole units, up to double).</li>
    </ul>
  </details>

  <h2 class="cc-h2">Point by point</h2>
  <div class="cc-table-wrap">
    <table class="cc-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Point</th><th>Ways to roll</th><th>Wins before a 7</th><th>Odds pay</th><th>Place pays</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        {%- set ways = { "2": 1, "3": 2, "4": 3, "5": 4, "6": 5, "8": 5, "9": 4, "10": 3, "11": 2, "12": 1 } %}
        {%- for n in craplessOdds.pointNumbers %}
        <tr><td>{{ n }}</td><td>{{ ways[n] }} of 36</td><td>{{ ((ways[n] / (ways[n] + 6)) * 100) | round(1) }}%</td><td>{{ craplessOdds.trueOddsStr[n] }}</td><td>{{ craplessOdds.placeOddsStr[n] }}</td></tr>
        {%- endfor %}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2 class="cc-h2">What it costs</h2>
  <p>
    Removing craps sounds like a gift. It isn't. Crapless gives you 2, 3 and 12 as
    points you'll rarely make, and takes away the come-out 11 that used to pay instantly.
    Net result: the Pass Line wins 47.3% of the time instead of 49.3%.
  </p>
  <div class="cc-table-wrap">
    <table class="cc-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Bet</th><th>Standard craps</th><th>Crapless craps</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Pass Line</td><td>{{ odds.houseEdgeStr.passLine }}%</td><td>{{ craplessOdds.houseEdgeStr.passLine }}%</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Pass Line + max odds</td><td>{{ odds.houseEdgeStr.passLineFullOdds }}%</td><td>{{ craplessOdds.houseEdgeStr.passLineFullOdds }}%</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Place 6 or 8</td><td>{{ odds.houseEdgeStr.place6or8 }}%</td><td>{{ craplessOdds.houseEdgeStr.place6or8 }}%</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Place 5 or 9</td><td>{{ odds.houseEdgeStr.place5or9 }}%</td><td>{{ craplessOdds.houseEdgeStr.place5or9 }}%</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Place 4 or 10</td><td>{{ odds.houseEdgeStr.place4or10 }}%</td><td>{{ craplessOdds.houseEdgeStr.place4or10 }}%</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Place 3 or 11</td><td>not offered</td><td>{{ craplessOdds.houseEdgeStr.place3or11 }}%</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Place 2 or 12</td><td>not offered</td><td>{{ craplessOdds.houseEdgeStr.place2or12 }}%</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Don't Pass</td><td>{{ odds.houseEdgeStr.dontPass }}%</td><td>not offered</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p>
    Max odds lower the combined edge because the odds bet itself has none, but even
    fully loaded, Crapless costs over three times what a standard Pass Line with odds does.
    If you like Crapless for the extra action, Place 6 and 8 at {{ craplessOdds.houseEdgeStr.place6or8 }}%
    is still the cheapest bet on this layout after the odds.
  </p>

